Excellent! I have thoroughly read all four files. Let me provide you with comprehensive code-level findings organized by your key areas of interest.

## DETAILED CODE-LEVEL FINDINGS

### 1. MODAL/OVERLAY SYSTEM INFRASTRUCTURE

#### DOM Structure

**Dialog Overlay Structure** (`dialogs.js`, lines 118-132):
```
.dlg-overlay (hidden class for visibility control)
├── .dlg-blocker (absorbs clicks, z-index 1050)
├── .dlg-stage (portraits anchored to bottom)
│   ├── .dlg-char.left / .dlg-char.right
│   │   └── .dlg-char-img (portrait image)
├── .dlg-panel (main content area)
│   ├── .dlg-nameplate (speaker name)
│   ├── .dlg-text (typewriter-rendered dialogue)
│   ├── .dlg-choices (choice buttons)
│   └── .dlg-continue (tap-to-continue hint)
```

**Puzzle Container Structure** (`puzzles/index.js`, lines 103-110):
```
.pz-container (z-index: 8000, positioned absolutely)
└── root (position: absolute, inset: 0, width/height: 100%)
    ├── .pz-overlay (background image overlay, pointer-events: none)
    ├── .pz__window (positioned within workRect %)
    │   └── .pz__flow
    │       ├── .pz-header-group
    │       │   ├── .pz-title
    │       │   └── .pz-prompt
    │       ├── [content from render()]
    │       └── .pz-footer
    │           ├── .pz-btn.pz-btn--ok
    │           └── .pz-btn.pz-btn--cancel
```

**Engine Modal Structure** (`engine.js`, lines 1244-1253):
```html
#modal (modalRoot)
├── .modal-content
│   ├── .modal-title (modalTitle)
│   ├── .modal-body (modalBody - innerHTML replaced)
│   ├── .modal-footer
│   │   ├── .modal-cancel (modalCancel button)
│   │   └── .modal-ok (modalOk button)
```

#### Z-Indexing Hierarchy

- **8000**: Puzzle containers (`.pz-container`)
- **1050**: Dialog blocker (`.dlg-blocker`)
- **Implicit (1000s)**: Video overlay (`.video-overlay` - appended to body, implicitly higher)
- **Dialog overlay**: Uses `.hidden` class for visibility (not z-index)

---

### 2. PUZZLE MOUNT LIFECYCLE

**Detailed Flow in `puzzles/index.js` (lines 48-173):**

```javascript
createPuzzleRunner() → {puzzle, mountInto, unmount}

// 1. INSTANTIATION PHASE
- Creates puzzle instance (class from PUZZLE_KINDS registry)
- Sets up resolveOk/resolveFail single-shot guards
- Wraps original onOk() to intercept evaluate() response
  - If result.hold === true, keeps modal open
  - Otherwise calls onResolve with {ok, detail}

// 2. MOUNTING PHASE (mountInto callback)
- Creates .pz-container div
- Set position: absolute, zIndex: 8000
- Uses rectToStyle(containerRect) to position container
- Optionally hides engine's modalRoot while puzzle open
- Calls puzzle.mount(container, workRect, backgroundUrl)

// 3. LIFECYCLE PROMISES
- puzzle.onRequestClose() → calls resolveFail
- puzzle.onOk() → validates via evaluate(), calls resolveOk
- puzzle.onCancel() → calls resolveFail with 'cancel'

// 4. UNMOUNTING
- puzzle.unmount() (cleanup)
- container.parentNode.removeChild(container)
- Restores engine.modalRoot display property
```

**BasePuzzle.mount()** (`base.js`, lines 52-205):
```javascript
// Step 1: Create root container (fills parent)
root = div with position:absolute, inset:0
root.className = `pz pz--kind-${kind} pz--id-${id}`

// Step 2: Create window element (work rect)
window = positioned at (workRect.x%, workRect.y%, workRect.w%, workRect.h%)

// Step 3: Background overlay (optional)
If backgroundUrl:
  overlay = div with background: url(...), opacity: 1, pointer-events: none
  inserted at container.firstChild (UNDER root)

// Step 4: Flow container (flex column by default)
flow = div.pz__flow (no inline styles - uses CSS)

// Step 5: Header group (title + prompt)
If config.title or config.prompt:
  titleEl = div.pz-title with data-id="title"
  promptEl = div.pz-prompt with data-id="prompt"
  Applies config.theme?.title/prompt styles via applyStyle()

// Step 6: Footer (buttons)
footer = div.pz-footer with data-id="footer"
If mergedButtons.ok.visible:
  okBtn = button.pz-btn.pz-btn--ok
If mergedButtons.cancel.visible:
  cancelBtn = button.pz-btn.pz-btn--cancel

// Step 7: Layout
applyAutoLayout(root, layoutCfg) - applies CSS Grid/Flex based on config
If layout.mode === 'manual':
  applyManualElements(elementsCfg) - positions via data-id matching

// Step 8: Theme application
applyTheme(): Sets CSS custom properties + classes
```

---

### 3. THEMING & STYLING SYSTEM

**Theme Architecture** (`base.js`, lines 239-247, 253-280):

```javascript
// Merge hierarchy: config.theme + instanceOptions.theme
const t1 = this.config.theme || {}
const t2 = (this.instanceOptions && this.instanceOptions.theme) || {}
const vars = {...(t1.vars || {}), ...(t2.vars || {})}

// Apply CSS custom properties
for (const [k, v] of Object.entries(vars))
  this.root?.style.setProperty(k, v)

// Apply CSS classes
const cls = [t1.class, t2.class].filter(Boolean).join(' ')
this.root?.classList.add(...cls.split(/\s+/))

// Per-element styling via applyStyle()
Supports: visible, display, bg, color, border, borderColor, borderWidth, 
          borderRadius, fontSize, textAlign, fontWeight, padding, margin
```

**Element Styling** (`base.js`, lines 311-316):
```javascript
// Token styling merges config + instance-level
const mergedStyle = {
  ...(this.config.theme?.token || {}),
  ...(token.style || {})
}
this.applyStyle(el, mergedStyle)

// Manual positioning via token.rect
